  "as_of": "2022-09-28",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would increase penalties for specified competition and consumer law breaches and make unfair terms in covered standard form contracts subject to civil penalties.",
   "For many corporate breaches, the maximum would be the greatest of $50 million, triple the benefit obtained, or, where unquantifiable, 30% of relevant adjusted turnover.",
   "The unfair contract reforms would begin after a 12-month transition and cover more small business contracts, while introducing specified financial market and insurance exclusions."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Relevant maximum penalties for individuals would increase from $500,000 to $2.5 million.",
   "Proposing, using or relying on unfair terms in covered consumer and small business contracts would be prohibited.",
   "Consumer law protections would cover small business contracts involving a party with fewer than 100 employees or annual turnover below $10,000,000.",
   "Turnover-based penalties would use the breach period, with a minimum calculation period of 12 months."
  ],
  "affected": "Consumers, small businesses and companies using standard contracts would be affected.",
